nodes.prompt:
Brand: {{brand.brand_name}} — {{brand.brand_summary}}
Voice: {{brand.voice_tone}}
Audience: {{brand.target_personas}}

Before: {{inputs.before}}
After: {{inputs.after}}
CTA: {{inputs.cta}}
Casting note: {{inputs.presenter}}

Write a 3-shot cut: shot 1 is the before state, silent. Shot 2 is the same place after, silent. Shot 3 is the same person turning to the lens and saying one line.

`actor` must pin identity down hard enough to repeat: apparent age, build, hair, face details, exact clothing including colour and fabric, and the specific room with named objects in it.

`before_frame_prompt` is a still-image prompt for shot 1: the person in that room in the before state. Name the objects that make it the before state. No camera brand names, no quality adjectives, no text.

`after_edit_prompt` is an EDIT instruction on that same frame. Start with "Same person, same clothes, same room, same camera position." then change only what the product changes. The camera has not moved.

`close_edit_prompt` is a second EDIT instruction on the after frame: the same person now looking straight into the lens, both eyes open, about to speak.

`cta_line` is what they say in shot 3, at most 14 words.

`on_screen_text`: exactly 3 captions, at most 4 words each. The first two must read as a pair.
